1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,217
Last time, the game remembered steps, standing and credits, and nothing else.

2
00:00:07,017 --> 00:00:11,365
If your story turned on something the crew found out,

3
00:00:11,815 --> 00:00:13,989
you had to fake it.

4
00:00:15,789 --> 00:00:20,137
Today the game learns to remember what the crew knows.

5
00:00:21,037 --> 00:00:24,950
And you'll see exactly where it writes that down.

6
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:30,498
A fact is a few plain words that you choose.

7
00:00:31,398 --> 00:00:33,572
The Gleaners broke a boat.

8
00:00:35,372 --> 00:00:38,415
The crew either knows it, or doesn't.

9
00:00:39,315 --> 00:00:42,359
You write it where they learn it,

10
00:00:42,809 --> 00:00:45,417
and again wherever the story asks.

11
00:00:47,217 --> 00:00:49,826
There are two ways to learn.

12
00:00:50,276 --> 00:00:54,189
An answer in a hail, or finishing a step.

13
00:00:55,089 --> 00:00:57,263
And two ways to ask.

14
00:00:57,713 --> 00:01:00,757
On an answer, or on a line.

15
00:01:02,557 --> 00:01:05,600
A fact belongs to the whole game,

16
00:01:06,050 --> 00:01:08,659
and it doesn't move anybody's standing.

17
00:01:09,859 --> 00:01:12,467
First, a fact from a step.

18
00:01:13,367 --> 00:01:17,715
This is one of my old leads, the second colony.

19
00:01:18,615 --> 00:01:20,354
I add one line.

20
00:01:20,804 --> 00:01:22,978
Then, learn, and the words.

21
00:01:24,778 --> 00:01:28,691
A then line can do more than one thing.

22
00:01:29,591 --> 00:01:32,200
Put a comma after the first,

23
00:01:32,650 --> 00:01:34,389
and write the second.

24
00:01:35,289 --> 00:01:40,072
So a step on your spine can reveal the next step,

25
00:01:40,522 --> 00:01:43,130
and teach a fact as well.

26
00:01:44,930 --> 00:01:48,409
This lead only teaches, so one is enough.

27
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:52,217
Second, a fact from a hail.

28
00:01:53,117 --> 00:01:55,726
The Gleaners get a new answer.

29
00:01:56,176 --> 00:01:58,785
Ask what became of the boats.

30
00:02:00,585 --> 00:02:05,367
After the semicolon, where a cost or a deed would go,

31
00:02:05,817 --> 00:02:08,426
I write learn, and the fact.

32
00:02:10,226 --> 00:02:13,270
And the answer needs somewhere to lead,

33
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:18,502
so I add their reply at the end of the file.

34
00:02:19,702 --> 00:02:21,441
Now the Compact asks.

35
00:02:22,341 --> 00:02:25,820
A new answer, report what the Gleaners said.

36
00:02:26,270 --> 00:02:30,183
And after it, if learned, and the same words.

37
00:02:31,983 --> 00:02:36,765
A crew that never asked the Gleaners never sees this answer.

38
00:02:38,565 --> 00:02:40,739
The reply has two lines.

39
00:02:41,639 --> 00:02:45,987
One for a crew that's been to the assay office,

40
00:02:46,437 --> 00:02:49,480
and one for a crew that hasn't.

41
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:52,554
I guard both of them,

42
00:02:53,004 --> 00:02:57,352
because a line with no guard can always be said.

43
00:02:59,152 --> 00:03:01,761
I save, and lint says clean.

44
00:03:02,661 --> 00:03:04,835
And lint does read facts.

45
00:03:05,285 --> 00:03:08,328
Misspell one, and it tells you which.

46
00:03:09,528 --> 00:03:11,267
Let's play it, then.

47
00:03:12,167 --> 00:03:15,646
I pay the levy and take a job,

48
00:03:16,096 --> 00:03:21,313
then I go to the breaking yard and ask about the boats.

49
00:03:23,113 --> 00:03:24,852
Now I go home.

50
00:03:25,752 --> 00:03:27,491
There's the new answer,

51
00:03:27,941 --> 00:03:31,420
and the Compact gives me the first line.

52
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:35,393
Out to the second colony.

53
00:03:36,293 --> 00:03:39,772
Nothing on the screen says I've learned anything.

54
00:03:40,222 --> 00:03:44,135
A fact is silent until something asks for it.

55
00:03:45,935 --> 00:03:48,978
Home once more, and I report again.

56
00:03:49,878 --> 00:03:52,487
And now it's the second line.

57
00:03:53,687 --> 00:03:57,165
Now I close the game, all of it,

58
00:03:57,615 --> 00:03:59,789
and I start it again.

59
00:04:01,589 --> 00:04:03,328
The answer's still there,

60
00:04:03,778 --> 00:04:07,257
and the line is still the second one.

61
00:04:08,157 --> 00:04:10,765
The crew still knows both facts.

62
00:04:12,565 --> 00:04:15,174
Same system, same credits, same standing.

63
00:04:16,374 --> 00:04:18,113
Here's where it's kept.

64
00:04:19,013 --> 00:04:22,057
The last five lines of the save

65
00:04:22,507 --> 00:04:24,680
are what the crew knows.

66
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:29,959
And look at a step of the story.

67
00:04:30,859 --> 00:04:33,033
A key, and a state.

68
00:04:33,483 --> 00:04:35,657
No title, and no text.

69
00:04:37,457 --> 00:04:40,935
I search for the name of my campaign,

70
00:04:41,385 --> 00:04:43,559
and it isn't in here.

71
00:04:45,359 --> 00:04:47,967
So the save isn't a spoiler.

72
00:04:48,867 --> 00:04:52,780
And when I change a step's words between evenings,

73
00:04:53,230 --> 00:04:55,839
the crew gets the new words.

74
00:04:57,039 --> 00:04:59,213
There are two more things.

75
00:05:00,113 --> 00:05:05,330
The number at the end of the save's name is its slot,

76
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:07,520
and there are six.

77
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:13,667
Each slot is its own campaign, in its own file.

78
00:05:14,567 --> 00:05:17,611
So two tables can play one universe,

79
00:05:18,061 --> 00:05:22,409
and you can keep a slot for your own walks.

80
00:05:24,209 --> 00:05:28,557
And a campaign that's been won isn't a dead save.

81
00:05:29,457 --> 00:05:33,804
Continue it, and the crew gets one card saying so.

82
00:05:34,704 --> 00:05:36,443
Then they fly on.

83
00:05:37,643 --> 00:05:41,991
The whole list of what's kept is on the page,

84
00:05:42,441 --> 00:05:45,485
and every row of it was measured.

85
00:05:47,285 --> 00:05:49,024
Now it's your turn.

86
00:05:49,924 --> 00:05:53,402
Write one fact the crew learns by asking,

87
00:05:53,852 --> 00:05:56,896
and one they learn by going somewhere.

88
00:05:58,696 --> 00:06:01,304
Put an answer behind the first,

89
00:06:01,754 --> 00:06:05,667
at a station they can always get back to.

90
00:06:06,567 --> 00:06:09,176
Then stop the game, come back,

91
00:06:09,626 --> 00:06:11,800
and check they still know.
